                                "sense_id": "63ecd289-1657-31d1-9b08-9e290e5a83c3",
                                "text": "...so far as my experience goes, all loricate Rotifera are hatched with the lorica already developed."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e7316a8d-e542-4ab2-9dde-0e38000fba7d",
                                "sense_id": "63ecd289-1657-31d1-9b08-9e290e5a83c3",
                                "text": "1891 William B.Carpenter, 7th ed rev. W.H.Dallinger. The Microscope and its Revelations. p. 718. pub: London J.&A. Churchill\nThe third order, Ploïma, is divided into a loricate and an illoricate group, which are not, however, very sharply separated; as in some cases the outer layer of the skin is, though horny, yet thin and flexible."
                            }
                        ]
